# Day 34

**34km / 9 hours**

Wretched. That's the word I would use to describe the day. If yesterday was long but pleasant then today was long but awful. This was entirely self-inflicted though since I had other options but foolishly pressed on. 

I decided to sleep in, both to rest up a bit in the morning and pack things up and also because i was hoping to be at the shops after 9am when they might open. However it's Labour Day which is a public holiday here so only big stores were open which scuppered that idea and just meant I was late to set off through the city. 

The city was not great to walk through, Hamilton is either a very town-like city or a city-like town, most likely the former at this point. This meant it was just not very interesting being similar to the places that had come before. It wasn't all road walking but even the sections that weren't just felt like parks of no great excitement. Even the Arboretum which sounds like it should be fascinating just felt like a bunch of trees.

![Some trees I guess](./arboretum.avif)

![The river alongside](./river.avif)

Some of the reasons I was so glum about the day was unrelated directly to the walk itself which I might elaborate on in a separate post. Anyway the path continued along road and farmland near the Waipā river which was alright until eventually there was a section where it was too early in the year since they were still lambing on the farmland which meant I had to take a detour entirely on the road. The road certainly wasn't designed for walking on so this was the last pleasant part of the day, perhaps the only nice part was a couple of shelters along the way to sit down in. 

![An automatic lawn mower, my only friend today](./automatic-mower.avif)

Late in the day I arrived at the place I would stay, my feet aching and feeling pretty down. Hopefully after a good night's sleep I'll be feeling better and full of vigour. I had a large pack today since I'm getting an inordinate amount of food so perhaps that contributed to the day.